==========================================================================
ASSESSMENT of 'the 7 impossibility'
==========================================================================
  LRC@14 = the 7 mod-7 classes never all-block. Near t=j/7 the 6 pair-classes are
  SAFE automatically (||cj/7||>=1/7); the whole problem collapses to clearing the
  SINGLETON {multiples of 7} in a small window. So the '7 impossibility' = the
  multiples-of-7 sub-system cannot block ALL SIX windows AND the bulk simultaneously.
  This is the constructive (S551) form of LRC@14: not a measure bound but explicit
  7-gon-vertex witnesses, with the residual = the small multiples-of-7 sub-LRC.
